            "paragraph": "The CaMa-Flood (Catchment-based Macro-scale Floodplain model, Yamazaki et al., 2011) is designed for large-scale flood risk analysis, simulating river discharge, water levels, and floodplain inundation while capturing hydrodynamic processes in continental rivers through local inertia equations that ensure efficient computation and retention of essential features such as storage and inundated extent.",
            "ontology_conformed": false,
